*  ONEWAY_driver - exercises ONEWAY(S).
*
*  NOTE ON THE CONTRACT.  ONEWAY.sno ships with NO header comment, so it has
*  no stated contract -- the manifest's contract_line for it is empty.  What
*  the module fixes on its own, without reading its body for behaviour: the
*  name and the -MODULE line say a one-way function of a string, and the
*  cases drive the two properties a one-way function has by definition --
*  the SAME input gives the SAME output (case 1 against case 2), and inputs
*  differing in one character give unrelated outputs (cases 3 and 4).  No
*  case asserts a particular digest value; the .ref records what the oracle
*  produces.
-INCLUDE "ONEWAY.sno"
        OUTPUT  =  ONEWAY('HELLO')
        OUTPUT  =  ONEWAY('HELLO')
        OUTPUT  =  ONEWAY('HELLP')
        OUTPUT  =  ONEWAY('JELLO')
        OUTPUT  =  ONEWAY('A')
        OUTPUT  =  ONEWAY('ABCDEFGHIJ')
END
